.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'At least one host-health observation originates off the host, so a dead host cannot silence its own observer'","No candidate signal (e.g. external reachability probe, synthetic canary, CloudWatch Synthetics) is named"],"finding":"AC2 requires 'at least one host-health observation originates off the host' but names neither the observation nor the off-box mechanism, leaving the executor to choose the health signal and its publisher.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1b3442dd35b37fa8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, second bullet","norm_id":"n9cf7487f3d7013e1","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must decide whether an off-box ping/HTTP canary, a Route53 health check, or a Lambda probe satisfies the criterion before building anything"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Name a concrete default (e.g. 'a CloudWatch Synthetics canary or external reachability check against the Gerrit endpoint') while leaving room to substitute an equivalent off-box observer.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the off-box logging path behaves under a hard host wedge (agent flush cadence / buffer loss), verify AC1 against an abrupt host loss rather than only a graceful source stop, and bound the residual unrecoverable window that get-console-output --latest is expected to cover.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2333,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Epic thesis: 'When the host degrades, the observation degrades with it -- and the failure that most needs explaining is precisely the one that destroys its own evidence.'","AC1 verification is 'after a source stops' (a clean stop); the child fab-dismal-haddock AC5 reads 'After an agent stop, the last lines remain readable' -- both exercise a graceful stop, not a hard host wedge / IOPS-saturation hang.","The CloudWatch agent runs ON the host and ships periodically; a kernel hang or IOPS-pinned host can lose the last batched window -- the same host-produces-its-own-signal property the epic is built to defeat.","ABSENCE: neither the epic nor the AC set states the agent's flush/buffer behaviour under degradation, nor bounds what remains unrecoverable beyond get-console-output --latest."],"finding":"The chosen off-box logging mechanism (a host-resident CloudWatch agent that ships journald/nginx logs in batches) partially inherits the very structural defect the epic names -- 'when the host degrades, the observation degrades with it' -- because the agent's final unflushed buffer during a hard wedge (the degradation window that most needs explaining) may never reach CloudWatch; the plan verifies only a clean source/agent stop, not the hard-wedge class it exists to explain, and does not bound the residual unrecoverable window.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7cf1a91eb680b717","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1 ('Host logs survive the host ... verified by reading the last lines from off-box after a source stops') and AC4 (console capture); cf. 'The distinction this epic turns on' / 'Every signal we have about the host is produced BY the host.'","norm_id":"n0d8e36270a37b391","priority":0.3667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future hard wedge like the 2026-09-04 41-min full-offline event: CloudWatch shows logs up to the last successful flush, then silence -- the final minutes of kernel/container evidence (the cause) are lost exactly as before.","IOPS saturation (the named cause) starves the agent's own disk writes/reads, delaying or dropping the final shipment."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC (or tighten AC1) that the capture story is evaluated under an abrupt host-loss scenario, not just a clean agent stop: name the agent's flush interval as the worst-case log-loss bound, and state explicitly that get-console-output --latest is the complementary capture for the final pre-wedge window, so the two together define what is and is not recoverable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a teardown / decommission path (as-code `terraform destroy`-able, and the Route 53 health check + SSM associations named) for the new off-box observability resources, consistent with the epic's cost-awareness stance.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Overlay check (g): 'Logging/metrics/alarms for new infra; reproducible as-code with a clear teardown.'","Epic AC1 specifies retention ('explicit, finite retention') and reproducibility is implicit (all Terraform-declared), but no criterion names how these resources are torn down / decommissioned if the pipeline is retired.","The epic itself flags retention cost ('Retention costs money ... a pattern not to inherit'), so an explicit teardown/lifecycle note is in keeping with its own cost stance."],"finding":"The epic provisions new durable AWS resources (a CloudWatch log group, an SSM parameter + two associations, an IAM policy, two alarms, and a Route 53 health check) but neither the epic acceptance criteria nor the child state a teardown / decommission path for them, which the Infra overlay's observability-&-ownership check calls for alongside reproducibility.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff231beadef4d8e11","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (epic) / child fab-dismal-haddock scope (infra/terraform/host_logs.tf)","norm_id":"n634424f552a05e5e","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The off-box log pipeline is later superseded or the host is retired, and the log group / health check / SSM associations linger as orphaned billed resources with no documented removal step."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a short note to the child scope (or a fifth epic AC) that the new resources are all Terraform-owned and removable via a single pl